{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "aurum-dictation-v1",
  "description": "Dictation-length STT corpus for the opencode-voice host contract (#11): 1-20 s clips, technical terms, hesitations, numbers, a quiet microphone, a noise floor, two non-US accents, and a silence false-positive clip.",
  "generator": "scripts/generate_dictation_corpus.sh",
  "generator_requirements": "macOS say (synthetic speech); no ffmpeg",
  "corpus_license": "CC0-1.0 (synthetic speech generated by the project; no human recordings)",
  "normalization": "aurum.dictation.normalize.v1",
  "budget": {
    "mean_wer_max": 0.25,
    "word_error_rate_max_any_clip": 0.6,
    "vocabulary_recall_min": 0.7,
    "silence_false_positives_max": 1,
    "silence_inserted_words_max": 1,
    "notes": "Baseline on tiny-q5_1 (metal, macOS arm64), 2026-11-07: mean WER 0.175, CER 0.079, vocabulary recall 0.769, mean RTF 0.40. Budgets carry headroom for one model step and for runner variance. The silence clip records a known whisper-tiny behaviour (it emits 'you' on digital silence through the file path); a dictation host gates on speech before calling transcribe, and the VAD work (#2) closes it. The cap fails on any second false positive or any longer hallucination."
  },
